23tz|a|One more than two; two and one.	j:1jh2,50,8;6tr,17,1;kmq,10,1;g3t,9,1;29oj,2,1;1l55,2,2;244n,1,2~1jh2,50,8;244n,1,2;1l55,2,2;kmq,10,1;g3t,9,1;6tr,17,1;29oj,2,1
23uf|n|The plank, stone, or piece of timber, which lies under a door, especially of a dwelling house, church, temple, or the like; the doorsill; hence, entrance; gate; door. ; Fig.: The place or point of entering or beginning, entrance; outset; as, the threshold of life.	a:17w6,56,10;bvs,45,4;1xnv,8,4~17w6,56,10;bvs,45,4;1xnv,8,4	v:1r6j,55,4~1r6j,55,4	n:1u7x,86,16~1u7x,86,16
23uf|v|The plank, stone, or piece of timber, which lies under a door, especially of a dwelling house, church, temple, or the like; the doorsill; hence, entrance; gate; door. ; Fig.: The place or point of entering or beginning, entrance; outset; as, the threshold of life.	s:1u7x,86,17~1u7x,86,17
